  <div class="main-content-container" style="z-index:5;position:relative;"><div style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;"><ix:nonNumeric id="F_ca7621c9-e416-4311-a49f-f81c9e5bdc17" contextRef="C_fcb8e15b-866a-4833-91bc-554da9f48273" name="us-gaap:AssetImpairmentChargesTextBlock" escape="true"><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="display:flex;margin-top:10pt;justify-content:flex-start;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:4.537%;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.537%;word-break:keep-all;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">10.</span><div style="display:inline;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Impairment Charges</span></div></div><p style="text-indent:4.533%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:10pt;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">The Company recorded impairment charges based on the difference between the carrying value of certain properties and their estimated fair market values totaling $</span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_6d84a329-2ef5-44bb-96f1-3eefa2a84cb7" contextRef="C_502869cf-9df5-492f-b9fd-abd4508ee777" name="sitc:ImpairedLongLivedAssetsHeldAndUsedFairValueDisclosure" unitRef="U_USD" scale="6" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">114.1</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> million and $</span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_aa537c89-943d-4605-8b9d-7ff8d4d1da9b" contextRef="C_e89a138c-3671-48df-b5f8-eda006984359" name="sitc:ImpairedLongLivedAssetsHeldAndUsedFairValueDisclosure" unitRef="U_USD" scale="6" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">66.6</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> million for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. The 2025 impairment charges recorded were triggered by a change in the hold period assumptions. The 2024 impairment charges recorded were triggered by a change in the hold period assumptions and these properties were subsequently sold in 2024.</span></p><div style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;"><ix:nonNumeric id="F_999e9989-1eb0-49d1-a833-abb83b13e90c" contextRef="C_fcb8e15b-866a-4833-91bc-554da9f48273" name="us-gaap:FairValueAssetsMeasuredOnNonrecurringBasisTextBlock" escape="true"><p style="text-indent:4.533%;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:10pt;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">The following table presents information about the fair value of real estate that was impaired, and therefore, measured on a fair value basis, along with the related impairment charge. The table also indicates the fair value hierarchy of the valuation techniques used by the Company to determine such fair value (in millions).</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </span></p>
